# Read by earlyoom.service via EnvironmentFile=-/etc/default/earlyoom, which is how the
# Fedora package expects to be configured. This file is %config(noreplace) and rpm-owned,
# so it is a full copy of the package default with only the changes below; the package's
# own version lands next to it as earlyoom.rpmnew, which the build deletes.
#
# Changed from the Fedora Workstation SIG default (pagure.io/fedora-workstation/issue/119):
#
#   -m 20,10   SIGTERM at 20% of earlyoom's "user mem total" (MemAvailable+AnonPages),
#              SIGKILL at 10%. The default -m 4 is far too late on this machine: headroom
#              for the app is ~17 GB against a 17-20 GB working set, so by 10% it is
#              already thrashing. 20% fires while the desktop is still responsive.
#   -M dropped The default -M 409600 caps the trigger at 400 MiB available, and earlyoom
#              uses the LOWER of -m and -M. Keeping it would pin the threshold at 400 MiB
#              and make -m 20,10 dead weight.
#   -s 100,100 Ignore swap entirely. earlyoom needs BOTH memory and swap below their
#              thresholds; with a 32 GiB swapfile, free swap would otherwise gate it off
#              and it would never fire. Both halves are required: a bare -s 100 leaves the
#              SIGKILL threshold at the PERCENT/2 default, so with swap more than 50% free
#              earlyoom would only ever escalate as far as SIGTERM.
#   --avoid    The SIG list, plus codehydra. --avoid matches /proc/PID/comm (first 15
#              bytes only, hence the truncated names) and subtracts 300 from oom_score, so
#              the victim is a build or a renderer rather than the compositor or the
#              Electron browser process.
#
# The point of earlyoom here is that it kills the single offending process. systemd-oomd
# cannot: it only kills whole cgroups (systemd RFE #25853), which on this machine took out
# all ~120 CodeHydra processes at once.
#
# More documentation at `man earlyoom` or `earlyoom -h`.

EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 0 -m 20,10 -s 100,100 --prefer '^(Web Content|Isolated Web Co)$' --avoid '^(dnf|packagekitd|gnome-shell|gnome-session-c|gnome-session-b|lightdm|sddm|sddm-helper|gdm|gdm-wayland-ses|gdm-session-wor|gdm-x-session|Xorg|Xwayland|systemd|systemd-logind|dbus-daemon|dbus-broker|cinnamon|cinnamon-sessio|kwin_x11|kwin_wayland|plasmashell|ksmserver|plasma_session|startplasma-way|sway|i3|xfce4-session|mate-session|marco|lxqt-session|openbox|cryptsetup|codehydra)$'"
